---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import PageHero from "../components/PageHero.astro";
---

<Base
  title="Markets"
  description="Some new turbine systems are five years out. TBES finds used units of all kinds, and connects specialists if you need assistance."
>
  <PageHero
    eyebrow="Markets"
    title="Some new turbine systems are five years out."
    lede="That wait is real for certain large frames. We still take all kinds of units. If you need assistance, we connect the specialists."
  />

  <section class="section">
    <div class="section-inner">
      <div class="split">
        <div class="stack">
          <h2>Data centers</h2>
          <p>
            Data center power demand is growing fast. Operators need generation that is reliable, flexible, and able to be deployed quickly, including when a building is ready before the grid is.
          </p>
          <p>
            Some of the new systems these sites are quoted are five years out. A used unit that specialists can bring back online can meet a date the building can actually use. Smaller and mid-size machines are part of the same search.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="stack">
          <p class="eyebrow">Who shows up</p>
          <ul class="check-list">
            <li>Data center developers</li>
            <li>Data center operators</li>
            <li>Colocation providers</li>
            <li>Hyperscale providers</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section alt">
    <div class="section-inner">
      <div class="split">
        <div class="stack">
          <h2>Industrial and manufacturing</h2>
          <p>
            Manufacturing and process plants tie power to output. When the load stops, the work stops. These sites need generation that can carry the plant or stand ready beside the utility supply.
          </p>
          <p>
            Industrial plants need power on a date they can use. Some new turbine systems are five years out. We find a used unit of whatever class fits the load. If you need assistance, we connect the specialists. The plant's engineers decide how it ties into the facility.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="stack">
          <p class="eyebrow">Who shows up</p>
          <ul class="check-list">
            <li>Industrial facilities</li>
            <li>Manufacturing plants</li>
            <li>Operators adding load or replacing on-site generation</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="section-inner">
      <div class="split">
        <div class="stack">
          <h2>Utilities and independent power producers</h2>
          <p>
            Utilities and independent power producers buy machines for a duty they already know: capacity, replacement, or a project built around a specific turbine or generator. They need a clear view of the asset and a transaction that can close.
          </p>
          <p>
            We locate candidate equipment, support verification, and manage the commercial path. We do not take the place of the project engineer.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="stack">
          <p class="eyebrow">Who shows up</p>
          <ul class="check-list">
            <li>Utilities</li>
            <li>Independent power producers</li>
            <li>Teams procuring a turbine or generator for a defined project</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section alt">
    <div class="section-inner">
      <div class="split">
        <div class="stack">
          <h2>Government and mission-critical infrastructure</h2>
          <p>
            Government facilities and other mission-critical sites plan for energy security and resilience. The standard is simple. The load is not supposed to go down.
          </p>
          <p>
            These organizations need proven equipment and a straight account of condition and history. We source the machine, support verification, and manage the transaction.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="stack">
          <p class="eyebrow">Who shows up</p>
          <ul class="check-list">
            <li>Government facilities</li>
            <li>Mission-critical site operators</li>
            <li>Owners planning resilient on-site power</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="cta-band">
    <div class="cta-inner">
      <h2>Name the load.</h2>
      <p>Tell us the kind of site, the machine class or the duty, and the timing.</p>
      <a class="btn btn-primary" href="/contact">Send an inquiry</a>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
